    "answer": {
      "short": "$34.4$ units, assuming $B$ lies between $A$ and $C$. Find $AB$ using the distance formula, then use $AC=\\frac{11}{4}AB$.",
      "worked": "Assuming $B$ lies between $A$ and $C$:\n$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=(7-(-4))^2+(-5-1)^2\\\\AB^2&=157\\\\AB&=\\sqrt{157}\\\\BC&=\\frac{7}{4}AB\\\\BC&=\\frac{7}{4}\\sqrt{157}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}AC&=AB+BC\\\\AC&=AB+\\frac{7}{4}AB\\\\AC&=\\frac{11}{4}AB\\\\AC&=\\frac{11}{4}\\sqrt{157}\\\\AC&\\approx34.4\\text{ units}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
